{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:0385fd5cb4ceb9c9","name":"Eldewn and Elsae Sarvool","source":{"id":"source:reference-0385fd5cb4ceb9c9","title":"Eldewn and Elsae Sarvool","revision":21567,"timestamp":"2024-08-26T02:02:50Z","sha256":"9d8db5c377c9f62a7dc634fc97ba371db1259f32334e7c71d8a16cf3cdd75e4e","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=21567","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=Eldewn%20and%20Elsae%20Sarvool&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-0385fd5cb4ceb9c9","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Web Enhancements"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Web_Enhancements"}," (",{"tag":"a","children":["Bounty Postings"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Bounty_Postings"},")"]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Eldewn and Elsae Sarvool are the children of a wealthy ",{"tag":"a","children":["Human"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Human","referenceId":"reference:9ffa865f2bc6e850"}," merchant who lived on the planet ",{"tag":"a","children":["Romin"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Romin?action=edit&redlink=1"},", located in ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Mid Rim"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Mid_Rim?action=edit&redlink=1"},". The impoverished planet was divided into two parts- one for the rich who hid behind thick durasteel walls, and one for the rest of the planet. As twins, the Sarvool children showed more than the usual \"Twin Thought\" common among those types of siblings.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["During a mission to help bring down a crime lord, a Jedi named ",{"tag":"a","children":["Ofar Tan-Doov"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Ofar_Tan-Doov?action=edit&redlink=1"}," discovered that the children were extremely powerful in ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Force"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Force","referenceId":"reference:67fe90e919b74d0f"},". He made an arrangement with their parents to take them back to ",{"tag":"a","children":["Coruscant"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Coruscant","referenceId":"reference:2ee37a21e9e7a955"}," for induction into the Order. Failing to capture the crime lord, Tan-Doov left the system to bring the children back to the temple on ",{"tag":"a","children":["Coruscant"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Coruscant","referenceId":"reference:2ee37a21e9e7a955"},". As his ship left the planet, an explosion from a hidden ",{"tag":"a","children":["Thermal Detonator"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Thermal_Detonator","referenceId":"reference:0cb8bf5b3c4e20e2"}," rocked the bridge, killing the Jedi. Eldewn and Elsae managed to get into escape pods, sending them hurtling back to the planet's surface. The twins survived and tried to make their way back home, but they soon discovered that their dwelling had been burned to the ground and their parents killed.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["The two quickly realized that the crime lord that the Jedi was sent to bring to justice had instigated the sabotage of the ship and their parents' murder. Knowing that there was no one else to trust, Eldewn and Elsae hid in the slums of ",{"tag":"a","children":["Romin"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Romin?action=edit&redlink=1"}," and blended into the populace. Living like street urchins, their anger grew, blaming both ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Jedi"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Jedi","referenceId":"reference:d320edb17de6c558"}," for taking them away from their parents and the criminal organization that was responsible for their death. Meanwhile, the crime boss created his own bounty to capture the children and use them as weight against other merchants on the planet. However, it's unclear whether he knew that the twins had such a powerful command of ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Force"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Force","referenceId":"reference:67fe90e919b74d0f"},".\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Now nine years old, Eldewn and Elsae are surprisingly tough and savvy individuals who constantly keep on the move, both to survive and to keep out of the clutches of anyone looking for them. ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Jedi"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Jedi","referenceId":"reference:d320edb17de6c558"}," have vowed to find the twins and bring them into the safety of the Order for training. The reports sent back by Tan-Doov before his death made it clear that their powers were truly potent and dangerous if not monitored.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h4","children":["Psych Profile"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Although still very young, Eldewn and Elsae are smart for their age and possess incredible knowledge of ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Force"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Force","referenceId":"reference:67fe90e919b74d0f"},". However, their fugitive lifestyle means that they spend most of their time living in the moment and keeping one step ahead of those who hunt them. They are suspicious, distrusting, and manipulative of others, doing what they can to get what they need and then moving on. Although they desperately want to find a safe place to stay, they know that they can't remain still, so they make no close ties. Eldewn and Elsae have been lying for so long that its become second nature, and it's difficult to get a true story out of them. \n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h4","children":["Eldewn and Elsae Sarvool by Era"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Depending on when your campaign takes place, you can include Eldewn and Elsae Sarvool in your adventures in a number of ways.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"ul","children":[{"tag":"li","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["The Old Republic Era"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Old_Republic_Era"},":"]}," In this era, Eldewn and Elsae are running from two different groups- ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Jedi"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Jedi","referenceId":"reference:d320edb17de6c558"}," who abandoned them and ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Sith"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Sith","referenceId":"reference:32bde5e69837ac8e"},", who want to bring them back to their academy on ",{"tag":"a","children":["Korriban"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Korriban","referenceId":"reference:e5de27f696051005"}," for indoctrination."]},"\n",{"tag":"li","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["The Clone Wars"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Clone_Wars"},":"]},"  Eldewn and Elsae can be found on any of the numerous planets devastated by war, hiding in the throngs of refugees and war victims fleeing from the conflict between the Separatists and the Republic. ",{"tag":"a","children":["Count Dooku"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Count_Dooku","referenceId":"reference:28558e49506f1132"}," (or another Sith Lord) could be one of the many people who have placed a bounty on their heads in hopes of capturing the twins for their own nefarious plans."]},"\n",{"tag":"li","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["The Dark Times"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Dark_Times"},"/",{"tag":"a","children":["The Rebellion Era"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Rebellion_Era"},":"]}," With the destruction of ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Jedi Order"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Jedi_Order"},", Eldewn and Elsae are in even more danger, as the Empire scours the galaxy for all kinds of Force-sensitive beings. Their young age makes them especially appealing to adherents of ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Dark Side"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Dark_Side"},", who would like to turn the twins into powerful minions."]},"\n",{"tag":"li","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["The New Jedi Order Era"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_New_Jedi_Order_Era"},":"]}," Left to their own devices, Eldewn and Elsae could eventually become a destabilizing factor in the delicate reconstruction of the Republic. Their backstory fits nicely with the goals and methods of the New Jedi Order, and Luke Skywalker himself could send bounty hunters (as well as his own students) to bring the children back to safety for training."]}]},"\n",{"tag":"h4","children":["Adventure Hooks"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Here are some ways to incorporate Eldewn and Elsae Sarvool into your adventures.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"ul","children":[{"tag":"li","children":["The twins board a tramp freighter or other ",{"tag":"a","children":["Starship"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Starship"}," leaving ",{"tag":"a","children":["Romin"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Romin?action=edit&redlink=1"}," and catch a ride to another planet. Regardless of where they go, they keep a low profile, blending in as much as possible, stealing food when necessary, and using their powers to stay alive."]},"\n",{"tag":"li","children":["The heroes are hired to investigate a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Romin"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Romin?action=edit&redlink=1"}," uprising of young orphans, street toughs, and other wretches who have banded together to create a huge gang. Someone has put a bounty on the leaders- a brother and sister who fit the description of Eldewn and Elsae. However, to collect the bounty, the heroes must bring in the twins unharmed."]}]},"\n","\n",{"tag":"p","children":["As twins, Eldewn and Elsae Sarvool effectively have the same statistics. They are always found together.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["Eldewn and Elsae Sarvool Statistics (CL 3 Each)"]},"\n",{"tag":"h4","children":["Normal"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Medium ",{"tag":"a","children":["Human"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Human","referenceId":"reference:9ffa865f2bc6e850"}," (Child) ",{"tag":"a","children":["Nonheroic"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Nonheroic","referenceId":"reference:1bca2ef1d9ebe1c3"}," 3/",{"tag":"a","